summary:
  A scheduled recording begins at the next half-minute look instead of at
  its own moment.

history:
  The schedule was looked at every 30 seconds and a start waited for the
  look. A recording set for 18:30 began at 18:30:09.8, and because what is
  recorded is the rest of its window, the file was 290 seconds of 300
  (measured 2026-11-11). A start that falls inside the coming period gets
  a timer set to its moment; the wait is worked out by
  RecLogic.startsWithin, and this is the line that makes it run.

target:
  package/contents/ui/RecordingEngine.qml

find:
          recStartTimer.restart();

replace:
          recStartTimer.stop();

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_recordingengine.qml::test_the_capture_starts_at_its_moment_and_asks_for_the_whole_window.
  Line-neutral.
